&lt;p&gt;The MongoDB Developer Tools team is a diverse group of contributors working together to help our users manage MongoDB at global scale. This includes building tools for MongoDB Atlas: our database as a service offering and fastest growing product which allows users to deploy fault-tolerant, globally distributed MongoDB clusters in just minutes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re seeking an experienced Software Engineer to join our Developer Tools Team within the Database Experience department. The team is responsible for tools which allow users to interact with their data and to understand the health and performance of their MongoDB deployments. The Developer Tools Team works on a variety of APIs and customer-facing UIs empowering MongoDB users to interact with their stored data, whether that’s on desktop via MongoDB Compass or in the browser via Atlas Data Explorer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is fully remote for a candidate based in the United States with US citizenship.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Is a full stack engineer with a willingness to take on both frontend tasks and backend tasks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with TypeScript, React, and Node.js&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Has experience with the design and architecture of a modern, scalable, high availability web application&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Has experience working with databases&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enjoys collaboration and being part of a team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Is approachable, curious, and intellectually honest&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Would enjoy chasing down difficult problems in a distributed environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Always strives to expand their knowledge&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Nice to Haves&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of database internals and tuning mechanisms, particularly indexing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with websocket based client to server communication&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with developing and supporting microservice based architectures using Kubernetes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About MongoDB&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;MongoDB is built for change, empowering our customers and our people to innovate at the speed of the market. We have redefined the data platform for the AI era, enabling builders to create, transform, and disrupt industries with software. MongoDB’s unified data platform, the most widely available, globally distributed data platform on the market, helps organizations modernize legacy workloads, embrace innovation, and unleash AI. Our cloud-native platform, MongoDB Atlas, is the only globally distributed, multi-cloud data platform and is available across AWS, Google Cloud, and Microsoft Azure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With offices worldwide and over 67,000 customers, including 75% of the Fortune 100 and AI-native startups, relying on MongoDB for their most important applications, we’re powering the next era of software.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our compass at MongoDB is our &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.mongodb.com/company&quot;&gt;Leadership Commitment,&lt;/a&gt; guiding how and why we make decisions, show up for each other, and win. It’s what makes us MongoDB.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To drive the personal growth and business impact of our employees, we’re committed to developing a supportive and enriching culture for everyone. &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.mongodb.com/company/blog/culture/employee-benefits-that-make-a-difference-at-mongodb&quot;&gt;From employee affinity groups, to fertility assistance and a generous parental leave policy&lt;/a&gt;, we value our employees’ wellbeing and want to support them along every step of their professional and personal journeys.&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.mongodb.com/blog/channel/culture&quot;&gt; Learn more about what it’s like to work at MongoDB&lt;/a&gt;, and help us make an impact on the world!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;MongoDB is committed to providing any necessary accommodations for individuals with disabilities within our application and interview process. To request an accommodation due to a disability, please inform your recruiter.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;MongoDB, Inc. provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any type and makes all hiring decisions without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state or local laws.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Req ID: 2273494846&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;MongoDB’s base salary range for this role is posted below. Compensation at the time of offer is unique to each candidate and based on a variety of factors such as skill set, experience, qualifications, and work location. Salary is one part of MongoDB’s total compensation and benefits package. Other benefits for eligible employees may include: equity, participation in the employee stock purchase program, flexible paid time off, 20 weeks fully-paid gender-neutral parental leave, fertility and adoption assistance, 401(k) plan, mental health counseling, access to transgender-inclusive health insurance coverage, and health benefits offerings. Please note, the base salary range listed below and the benefits in this paragraph are only applicable to U.S.-based candidates.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;MongoDB’s base salary range for this role in the U.S. is:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$85,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$230,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The Kubernetes teams make running MongoDB in and from Kubernetes so frictionless that it is the default database choice for cloud-native applications. Our operators let developers and platform teams provision, scale and operate MongoDB through Kubernetes-native APIs, in their own clusters or in MongoDB Atlas.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will join the Kubernetes Capabilities squad. Our sister squad builds the shared platform layer of the MongoDB Controllers for Kubernetes; we build the capabilities on top of it that users actually adopt. That means bringing MongoDB features such as Search and Vector Search to Kubernetes, extending what our users can deploy and manage declaratively, and owning the Atlas Kubernetes Operator. Our work starts with a user problem and ends with a Kubernetes API that solves it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In practice, we build a platform for other engineers. Our users are developers and platform teams who expect self-service, sensible defaults and APIs that behave predictably. If you have built an internal developer platform, a Kubernetes controller, or any system whose customers are other engineers, you will recognise the problems we work on.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;No prior experience with MongoDB is required. You will meet most of the team during interviews, and we pride ourselves on being an inclusive, collaborative group that Builds Together. Our core engineering values are Context, Predictability, Transparency, Focus and Craftsmanship.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role can be based in our Dublin office, Cork office or remotely within Ireland.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;The role&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Software Engineer to join the Kubernetes Capabilities squad and help decide which MongoDB capabilities our users get on Kubernetes and how they work. You will own significant capabilities from design to production, make sound technical decisions under ambiguity, and raise the engineering bar of the team through design, review and mentorship.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Experience we value&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;What matters most is that you have built platforms, not only operated them. We value experience from any of these backgrounds:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Building Kubernetes controllers, operators, CRDs, admission webhooks or other extensions against the Kubernetes API&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Building internal developer platforms: self-service provisioning, golden paths, platform APIs, CLIs or developer portals used by other engineering teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Building developer-facing infrastructure products such as SDKs, managed services, CI/CD systems or cloud provisioning tooling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the design and delivery of new capabilities in our Kubernetes operators, from technical design through production support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Product and the teams behind MongoDB features to turn them into Kubernetes-native APIs our users can adopt&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write technical designs that weigh trade-offs clearly and bring the team and stakeholders to a decision&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape our platform APIs with our users in mind: predictable, self-service and safe to operate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor engineers through pairing, code review and design feedback&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with our platform squad, Support, Docs and other engineering teams, and help resolve complex customer issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve how the team works, including testing strategy, release quality and developer experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong core software engineering skills and several years building production software in a modern language; we mostly use Go&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience building a platform for other engineers, such as Kubernetes controllers and operators, an internal developer platform, or developer-facing infrastructure products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep working knowledge of Kubernetes, including its API model, reconciliation and the operational realities of running workloads on it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing, testing and operating distributed systems in production&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of leading projects through ambiguity and delivering them end to end&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written communication, including technical design documents&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Nice to have&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with controller-runtime, kubebuilder or contributing to Kubernetes ecosystem projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with multi-cluster Kubernetes, networking or service mesh&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience running stateful workloads or databases on Kubernetes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with a major public cloud provider&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What is in it for you&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous compensation package (top-range salary, equity, comprehensive benefits)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A diverse, highly collaborative team that values shipping fast and clean&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Time to learn on the job and grow into new technologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A high level of independence, focused on results rather than the appearance of work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About MongoDB&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;MongoDB is built for change, empowering our customers and our people to innovate at the speed of the market. We have redefined the data platform for the AI era, enabling builders to create, transform, and disrupt industries with software. MongoDB’s unified data platform, the most widely available, globally distributed data platform on the market, helps organizations modernize legacy workloads, embrace innovation, and unleash AI. Our cloud-native platform, MongoDB Atlas, is the only globally distributed, multi-cloud data platform and is available across AWS, Google Cloud, and Microsoft Azure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With offices worldwide and over 67,000 customers, including AI-native startups and approximately 75% of the Fortune 100, relying on MongoDB for their most important applications, we’re powering the next era of software.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our compass at MongoDB is our &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.mongodb.com/company&quot;&gt;Leadership Commitment,&lt;/a&gt; guiding how and why we make decisions, show up for each other, and win. It’s what makes us MongoDB.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To drive the personal growth and business impact of our employees, we’re committed to developing a supportive and enriching culture for everyone. &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.mongodb.com/company/blog/culture/employee-benefits-that-make-a-difference-at-mongodb&quot;&gt;From employee affinity groups, to fertility assistance and a generous parental leave policy&lt;/a&gt;, we value our employees’ wellbeing and want to support them along every step of their professional and personal journeys.&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.mongodb.com/blog/channel/culture&quot;&gt; Learn more about what it’s like to work at MongoDB&lt;/a&gt;, and help us make an impact on the world!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;MongoDB is committed to providing any necessary accommodations for individuals with disabilities within our application and interview process. To request an accommodation due to a disability, please inform your recruiter.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;MongoDB is an equal opportunities employer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Req ID: 3273603861&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;MongoDB is growing faster than it has in years, with strong momentum in Atlas and EA. We are consolidating global Revenue Marketing under one leader to strengthen our partnership with Sales and build a modern, AI-powered revenue growth engine.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The SVP of Revenue Marketing owns marketing-sourced revenue for our sales-led business across AMER, EMEA, and APJ, including new investments in India, Japan, and Public Sector. You will rethink how we generate growth, connecting account intelligence, enterprise demand creation, developer engagement, and sales execution into a scalable system that influences architecture decisions and converts demand into revenue. You will also own partner marketing, digital services, and MDF.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role reports to the CMO, sits on the Marketing Leadership Team, and partners directly with the CRO. This is a revenue role that lives in marketing. You know why pipeline is short before anyone asks, and you act.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role can be based out of any of our US offices or remotely in the United States.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What you will own&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Marketing-sourced revenue: Own the sales-led marketing revenue target, regional forecasts, and performance; Anticipate pipeline gaps, diagnose performance, and adjust investment and execution to deliver the number&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Global revenue growth system: Build a unified growth engine across AMER, EMEA, and APJ; Move beyond traditional campaign- and event-centric execution toward always-on, signal-driven engagement; Establish repeatable growth plays, shared capabilities, and measurement while enabling regional teams to adapt to local markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enterprise demand and architecture decisions: Build account-based growth motions that engage executives, architects, and technical buyers early in their decision-making; Partner with Sales and technical teams to position MongoDB for new application and AI architectures, turning strategic account engagement into qualified pipeline and revenue&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI and automation: Partner across Marketing to redesign workflows, automate execution, and improve targeting, personalization, and optimization; Use AI to increase speed and impact while freeing teams for higher-value work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner marketing: Own hyperscaler, GSI, and OEM co-marketing, including MDF; Build scalable partner growth motions and tie investment to pipeline and revenue&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;New market growth: Build scalable market-entry and expansion models for India, Japan, and Public Sector, leveraging global capabilities and local market expertise&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What we&#39;re looking for&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Revenue accountability: You’ve owned and delivered a meaningful marketing-sourced revenue target at a B2B SaaS company operating at scale, across multiple regions and segments; You have experience navigating complex enterprise sales motions and driving predictable revenue growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commercial credibility: You’re a trusted partner to a CRO, experienced in enterprise account strategy, complex sales cycles, and expansion motions; You know how to diagnose pipeline gaps and drive corrective action&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Systems thinking: You&#39;ve redesigned how marketing generates growth, not just optimized existing campaigns; You connect data, technology, workflows, and people into scalable revenue motions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI fluency: You understand how AI and automation can transform marketing execution and have translated new capabilities into measurable business outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Global leadership: You&#39;ve led large, distributed teams and strong regional leaders, including meaningful APJ experience; You balance global scale with local execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ecosystem experience: You&#39;ve worked with hyperscalers and GSIs and know how to translate partnerships into pipeline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enterprise and technical buyer expertise: You’ve built demand and driven growth in complex enterprise sales motions, engaging C-suite executives, architects, and technical buyers; You understand how to connect developer adoption to enterprise platform decisions and navigate long, multi-stakeholder buying cycles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plus: Experience with data platforms, AI workloads, new market development, Japan, or Public Sector&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;How we&#39;ll measure success&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Marketing-sourced revenue: Pipeline through closed-won, against global and regional targets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pipeline performance: Conversion, velocity, and qualified pipeline in strategic accounts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Revenue efficiency: Marketing-sourced revenue and pipeline per dollar invested, including partner ROI&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Growth system effectiveness: Adoption and performance of repeatable, signal-driven revenue motions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI and automation: Measurable improvements in execution speed, productivity, and program performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategic growth: Qualified pipeline and revenue from new application and AI architectures, penetration of strategic enterprise accounts, and new market performance in India, Japan, and Public Sector&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About MongoDB&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;MongoDB is built for change, empowering our customers and our people to innovate at the speed of the market. We have redefined the data platform for the AI era, enabling builders to create, transform, and disrupt industries with software. MongoDB’s unified data platform, the most widely available, globally distributed data platform on the market, helps organizations modernize legacy workloads, embrace innovation, and unleash AI. Our cloud-native platform, MongoDB Atlas, is the only globally distributed, multi-cloud data platform and is available across AWS, Google Cloud, and Microsoft Azure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With offices worldwide and over 67,000 customers, including AI-native startups and approximately 75% of the Fortune 100, relying on MongoDB for their most important applications, we’re powering the next era of software.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our compass at MongoDB is our &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.mongodb.com/company&quot;&gt;Leadership Commitment,&lt;/a&gt; guiding how and why we make decisions, show up for each other, and win. It’s what makes us MongoDB.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To drive the personal growth and business impact of our employees, we’re committed to developing a supportive and enriching culture for everyone. &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.mongodb.com/company/blog/culture/employee-benefits-that-make-a-difference-at-mongodb&quot;&gt;From employee affinity groups, to fertility assistance and a generous parental leave policy&lt;/a&gt;, we value our employees’ wellbeing and want to support them along every step of their professional and personal journeys.&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.mongodb.com/blog/channel/culture&quot;&gt; Learn more about what it’s like to work at MongoDB&lt;/a&gt;, and help us make an impact on the world!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;MongoDB is committed to providing any necessary accommodations for individuals with disabilities within our application and interview process. To request an accommodation due to a disability, please inform your recruiter.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;MongoDB, Inc. provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any type and makes all hiring decisions without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state or local laws.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Req ID: 426495&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;MongoDB’s base salary range for this role is posted below. Compensation at the time of offer is unique to each candidate and based on a variety of factors such as skill set, experience, qualifications, and work location. Salary is one part of MongoDB’s total compensation and benefits package. Other benefits for eligible employees may include: equity, participation in the employee stock purchase program, flexible paid time off, 20 weeks fully-paid gender-neutral parental leave, fertility and adoption assistance, 401(k) plan, mental health counseling, access to transgender-inclusive health insurance coverage, and health benefits offerings. Please note, the base salary range listed below and the benefits in this paragraph are only applicable to U.S.-based candidates.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;MongoDB’s base salary range for this role in the U.S. is:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$213,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$419,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Elastic, the Search AI Company, enables everyone to find the answers they need in real time, using all their data, at scale — unleashing the potential of businesses and people. The Elastic Search AI Platform, used by more than 50% of the Fortune 500, brings together the precision of search and the intelligence of AI to enable everyone to accelerate the results that matter. By taking advantage of all structured and unstructured data — securing and protecting private information more effectively — Elastic’s complete, cloud-based solutions for search, security, and observability help organizations deliver on the promise of AI.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What is The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;p&quot; data-block=&quot;true&quot; data-editor=&quot;1hfcl&quot; data-offset-key=&quot;crj0u-0-0&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;public-DraftStyleDefault-block public-DraftStyleDefault-ltr&quot; data-offset-key=&quot;crj0u-0-0&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-offset-key=&quot;crj0u-0-0&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-text=&quot;true&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for a Cinematographer / Video Editor who is equally at home behind the camera and in the edit bay. You&#39;ll join Elastic&#39;s in-house video team, reporting to the Video Creative Lead, and help drive the look of our live-action work from the first lighting setup to the final export.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;p&quot; data-block=&quot;true&quot; data-editor=&quot;1hfcl&quot; data-offset-key=&quot;6af43-0-0&quot;&gt;
