&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Ready to do the most impactful work of your career? &lt;span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coinbase.com/?utm_campaign=mt_o_m_w_m_m__coi_0_jd-onchain&amp;amp;utm_source=coinbase&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Coinbase&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; is building the future of finance for people, institutions and their agents, with one place to trade crypto, equities, derivatives and prediction markets, use stablecoins, and connect AI agents with clear controls. The bar is high and the pace is intense, and we like it that way. This isn’t a place for complacency. It’s a place to be pushed past your perceived limits and do the best work of your career. If you’re ready to build the future of finance with a championship team who refuse to settle for “good enough,” you belong here. Coinbase is a remote-first, but not remote-only company. Expect to get together quarterly for in-person working sessions&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;As a Specialist, Market Operations, you&#39;ll provide frontline operational support across two exchanges: the Coinbase Derivatives Exchange (CDE) and Deribit. This team runs 24/7, keeping trading, clearing, and connectivity systems healthy for clients and internal stakeholders. You&#39;ll troubleshoot issues in real time, coordinate cross-functional resolution for complex problems, and execute deployment testing to protect production environments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;What you&#39;ll do:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own real-time functional and technical support for electronic trading, clearing systems, and exchange applications across CDE and Deribit.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Investigate and resolve customer inquiries related to exchange functionality, market events, connectivity, product schedules, and business technology.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide front-line support for internal and external investigations tied to exchange operations, including error trade analysis and resolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with product and development teams to launch new products, implement platform updates, and execute deployment testing in pre-production environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support onboarding and ongoing operational enablement of clients and vendors across both exchanges, including prediction markets and event contracts listed on CDE.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify, document, and recommend operational process improvements aligned with business objectives and platform growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Required Skills and Experience:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BA/BS in Information Systems, Economics, Finance, or a technical field, with 1+ years of experience in financial markets operations or a technical operations role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated product and operational knowledge of listed futures or options, including hands-on experience with error trade analysis and resolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to diagnose and articulate complex technical problems and solutions to both technical and non-technical audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience delivering multi-channel support (voice, email, chat) with documented ability to maintain quality under high-volume, time-sensitive conditions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with prediction markets, event contracts, FIX protocol, network protocols, SQL, or CRM tools such as Salesforce and JIRA is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Utilizes generative AI responsibly, maintaining human oversight to deliver business-ready outputs and drive measurable improvements in workflow efficiency, cost, and quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-Remote&lt;/p&gt;
